==Trivia ==
*Cat Bros, as well as [[Kabuto Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kabuto Cat]] and [[Kuwagata Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Kuwagata Cat]], is currently the only Switch-Exclusive cats to receive a [[Cat Bros (Rare Cat)|mobile counterpart]].
** Its counterpart has the [[Resistant]] ability against [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies as well as a different outfit in its evolved form.
*Cat Bros shares the exact same name with its mobile counterpart and the [[Cat Bros (Special Cat)|serial code unit]].
*It and [[Corodragon (Switch Special Cat)|Corodragon]] has had the most distributions in serial codes having three total distributions.
**The three distributions for Cat Bros were of the following:
***Launch period of The Battle Cats Unite in Japan.
***Versus Mode Limited Edition Soft Pouch Set release.
***Package Version Bonus set.
*Cat Bros is among the few Special Cats in the Nintendo Switch version to receive "+" levels, however it has the lowest cap, only being at +1.
*During the 「次世代ワールドホビーフェア'19 Winter」event, you could purchase a plush set of the Cat Bros, each purchase came with a free Platinum Ticket.
*It, [[Mallet Cat (Switch Special Cat)|Mallet Cat]], and the [[Rare Capsule Bonus Characters|Grandon Mining Corps]] are currently the only serial code units to be available in the '''Japanese''' and '''Southeast Asia''' versions of the game.
*It and Mallet Cat are the most expensive Switch-Exclusive Cats as the Official Limited Time Edition The Battle Cats Unite Combo Case went for 3500円 and the Package Version Bonus going for 2420円.

